  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe upward bias during high-volatility regimes; when the last 3 days show a price spike (e.g., >89 EUR) followed by mixed sentiment, the model underestimates the subsequent upside potential by 5-10%.",
    "The model fails to capture mean reversion after sharp spikes; it assumes linear growth from recent highs, whereas true outcomes frequently reverse direction within 3-5 days of a peak.",
    "Sentiment history is largely ignored by the model; periods with low sentiment (0.00) coinciding with price volatility result in significantly higher realized returns than predicted.",
    "The forecast horizon is too smooth and lacks intra-period variance; actual outcomes show high frequency oscillations around the trend line that the model averages out completely.",
    "When the last 18 days of history are clustered between 77-85 EUR, the model predicts a steady climb to ~90 EUR, but true outcomes often overshoot to >95 EUR before correcting."
  ]
}
